# Planets architecture (pointer)

Full law: [`docs/docs/architecture/planets.md`](../../docs/docs/architecture/planets.md).

**Permanent decision:** one **PlanetDocument** owns the body recipe (radius,
gravity, atmosphere shell, terrain, sky, surface life-support). Star Map
places the body (`planetId`); **Build Web** ships planets (not Console
catalog). Planet Authoring has a **Presets** dropdown (**10** named recipes)
and a **Random** button that rolls a saveable recipe (editor-only; not a
player runtime roll). Outdoor walk / run / jump **scale with planet *g***;
sealed interiors stay ~1g. One **active** planet owns
terrain + sky + atmospheric *g*; far bodies place + nav-blip. Sky /
`atmosphereHeightMeters` ≠ breathable.
[Star Map](../../docs/docs/architecture/star-map.md),
[Space traversal](../../docs/docs/architecture/space-traversal.md),
[Player](../../docs/docs/architecture/player.md),
[Home Worlds](../../docs/docs/architecture/home-worlds.md),
[Ship flight](../../docs/docs/architecture/ship-flight.md).

When changing planet schema, Planet Authoring (including **Presets** / **Random**),
active-planet handoff, surface vitals fields, outdoor on-foot *g* scaling, or
gas-giant vs rocky body rules, read the full doc first. Also listed in
`AGENTS.md`.
